<title>USA: Southwest, Icelandair expand agreement.</title>
<headline>Southwest, Icelandair expand agreement.</headline>
<dateline>DALLAS, Texas 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Southwest Airlines and Icelandair said on Thursday that they had expanded a marketing agreement to provide service from three new U.S. airports to Iceland and beyond.</p>
<p>The current agreement provides service from Cleveland, Ohio, to Baltimore and on to Iceland, the two carriers said in a statement, whereas the new arrangement will also provide a link for customers flying from Chicago Midway, Louisville and Providence.</p>
<p>The carriers also announced a roundtrip fare of $298 from the new locations to Luxembourg between November 1 and December 11.</p>
</text>
